# RetailMart KPI Catalog

## Purpose

This document defines the standardized Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)
used across the RetailMart analytics platform.

The purpose of this KPI catalog is to ensure that Sales, Finance,
Inventory, Management and BI teams use consistent business definitions
and calculations across reports and dashboards.

---

# 1. Total Sales

### KPI Name
Total Sales

### Definition
Total monetary value of sales generated during the selected period.

### Formula
SUM(sales_amount)

### Business Purpose
Measures the overall sales performance of RetailMart.

### Source Table
fact_sales

### Grain
One product line within one order.

### Business Owner
Sales / Finance


---

# 2. Total Orders

### KPI Name
Total Orders

### Definition
Total number of unique customer orders generated during the selected period.

### Formula
COUNT(DISTINCT order_id)

### Business Purpose
Measures transaction volume and helps understand customer purchasing activity.

### Source Table
fact_sales

### Grain
One product line within one order.

### Business Owner
Sales


---

# 3. Quantity Sold

### KPI Name
Quantity Sold

### Definition
Total number of product units sold during the selected period.

### Formula
SUM(quantity)

### Business Purpose
Measures product sales volume and helps identify high-demand products.

### Source Table
fact_sales

### Grain
One product line within one order.

### Business Owner
Sales / Inventory


---

# 4. Total Profit

### KPI Name
Total Profit

### Definition
Total profit generated from completed sales after considering the cost
associated with the products sold.

### Formula
SUM(profit_amount)

### Business Purpose
Measures the absolute profitability generated by RetailMart.

### Source Table
fact_sales

### Grain
One product line within one order.

### Business Owner
Finance


---

# 5. Profit Margin %

### KPI Name
Profit Margin %

### Definition
Percentage of sales revenue retained as profit after accounting for
the cost of goods sold.

### Formula
(Total Profit / Total Sales) × 100

### Business Purpose
Measures profitability efficiency and helps management compare
profitability across products, stores and categories.

### Source Table
fact_sales

### Grain
Calculated from aggregated sales data.

### Business Owner
Finance


---

# 6. Average Order Value (AOV)

### KPI Name
Average Order Value (AOV)

### Definition
Average monetary value generated by each customer order.

### Formula
Total Sales / Total Orders

### Business Purpose
Measures the average value of a customer transaction and helps
identify opportunities to increase basket size.

### Source Table
fact_sales

### Grain
Order level after aggregating product-line transactions.

### Business Owner
Sales / Marketing


---

# 7. Sales Growth %

### KPI Name
Sales Growth %

### Definition
Percentage change in sales between the current comparison period
and the previous comparison period.

### Formula
((Current Period Sales - Previous Period Sales)
 / Previous Period Sales) × 100

### Business Purpose
Measures sales performance over time and identifies growth or decline.

### Source Table
fact_sales + dim_date

### Grain
Time-period level, such as Month, Quarter or Year.

### Business Owner
Sales / Finance


---

# 8. Return Rate %

### KPI Name
Return Rate %

### Definition
Percentage of orders that were returned during the selected period.

### Formula
(Returned Orders / Total Orders) × 100

### Business Purpose
Measures the level of product returns and helps identify potential
product, quality or customer-experience issues.

### Source Table
fact_returns + fact_sales

### Grain
Order level.

### Business Owner
Sales / Quality / Operations


---

# 9. Customer Count

### KPI Name
Customer Count

### Definition
Number of unique customers who made at least one purchase during
the selected period.

### Formula
COUNT(DISTINCT customer_id)

### Business Purpose
Measures the active customer base and supports customer segmentation
and customer growth analysis.

### Source Table
fact_sales

### Grain
Customer level after aggregation.

### Business Owner
Sales / Marketing


---

# 10. Repeat Customer %

### KPI Name
Repeat Customer %

### Definition
Percentage of customers who placed two or more completed orders
during the selected analysis period.

### Formula
(Repeat Customers / Total Customers) × 100

### Business Purpose
Measures customer retention and purchasing loyalty.

### Source Table
fact_sales + dim_customer

### Grain
Customer level.

### Business Owner
Marketing / Sales


---

# 11. Available Inventory

### KPI Name
Available Inventory

### Definition
Total quantity of products currently available for sale after
excluding inventory that has already been reserved.

### Formula
SUM(stock_quantity - reserved_quantity)

### Business Purpose
Helps inventory and store managers monitor available stock and
identify potential inventory shortages.

### Source Table
fact_inventory

### Grain
One product per store/warehouse per inventory snapshot date.

### Business Owner
Inventory / Operations


---

# 12. Stock-Out Rate %

### KPI Name
Stock-Out Rate %

### Definition
Percentage of active products that are unavailable for sale
because their available inventory is zero.

### Formula
(Out-of-Stock Products / Total Active Products) × 100

### Business Purpose
Measures product availability and helps identify inventory
management problems.

### Source Table
fact_inventory + dim_product

### Grain
Product-store/warehouse snapshot level.

### Business Owner
Inventory / Operations





















































